<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azd</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Azd were a major group of Arab tribes originating in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a>. After migrations that tradition links with the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib">Marib</a> dam, branches settled across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>: the Ghassanids in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, the Aws and Khazraj in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, and others in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, where the Azd became dominant. In the early Islamic period Azd tribesmen were prominent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a> and Khurasan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azd.jpg" alt="Azd" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MWahaiibii · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Azd_Flag_(11).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
